.TH CHTTPCLI_SET_ENGINE_LOGGER 3 "2026-07-14" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_set_engine_logger \- set the logger for chttpclient's async-engine diagnostics
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpcli_set_engine_logger(clog cl);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Derives a child logger from cl, adds the field
component=http-client-engine, and installs it as the shared Tier 2/3
async engine's diagnostics logger.  Any previously installed engine
logger is closed.

chttpclient_do_async/_streaming and the pooled-sync wrappers built on
top of them (chttpclient_do_pooled/_streaming) share one lazily-started,
process-wide event_loop reactor across every chttpcli instance in the
process, including the default client.  This function captures that
reactor's own diagnostics (TLS handshake failures, connect errors); it
is separate from the per-client logger, and separate from
chttpsvr_set_engine_logger's own reactor (chttpserver and chttpclient
each own a fully independent static reactor; a process may freely run
both at once).

Call this before the first chttpclient_do_async/_streaming call
anywhere in the process if a custom engine logger is wanted.  If no
logger has been installed when the engine first starts, a fallback
logger (fd 2, level CLOG_FATAL) is installed automatically; since
this engine's own diagnostics are never logged above CLOG_INFO, that
fallback logger is silent in practice unless this function is used
to install a more verbose one.

cl must not be NULL; the derived child logger is owned by the engine
and must not be closed by the caller.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args if cl is NULL.
ccol_not_enough_memory if the child logger cannot be allocated.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_logger (3)
